==Battleground==
*5 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*4 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is practically ''impossible'' without any [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal units]], making it hard to go in blind. To beat the stage, you must use cats that have at least a somewhat reliable [[Critical Hit]] chance, like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]. Bulky Critical Hitters, like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] can help as well, but it is suggested that you use something better with them, because they have a low Critical chance. If you have any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] that can do Criticals, like [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Marauder Cat]], [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]], or [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]], feel free to use them. [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]], if you have it, is the best attacker here, due to its incredibly fast attack rate allowing it to perform Critical Hits over and over again. Catornado's Critical Hits will OHKO every enemy here except the Super Metal Hippoe. Notably, [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tecoluga]] can one-hit KO every enemy here, but his critical rate of 20% (in True Form) and the overabundant spam of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]] do not bode well for it overall. [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] can be good here.

